  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Primary path (Regular mode)",
      "items": [
        "POST /v1/chat/completions is authorized (if configured), then RouterTrait.route_chat selects one worker and proxies the request.",
        "RouterFactory builds Router, VllmPDRouter, or OpenAIRouter from RoutingMode. A worker pool is all HTTP or all grpc://; mixed schemes are rejected.",
        "gRPC workers receive tokenizer-prepared token_ids; HTTP workers are reverse-proxied as OpenAI/vLLM JSON. Default listen address is 127.0.0.1:30000."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Prefill / Decode disaggregation",
      "items": [
        "In vLLM PD mode the router admits a P/D pair, then runs Stage 1 prefill and Stage 2 decode over HTTP or gRPC, injecting kv_transfer_params. A P/D pool is all HTTP or all grpc://; mixed schemes are rejected.",
        "NIXL is the default connector; Mooncake and MoRI-IO are also supported. When a NIXL push identity is cached, or MoRI-IO WRITE is used, P and D may be dispatched concurrently.",
        "KV cache bytes move worker-to-worker. The router only coordinates identities and transfer metadata."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Policies and KV Index",
      "items": [
        "Default policy is cache_aware. Also supported: random, round_robin, power_of_two, kv_aware, consistent_hash, sticky_least_loaded, rendezvous_hash.",
        "PD mode can override prefill and decode policies independently. kv_aware consults the KV Index (engine events, SHA-256 block hashes) for tiered placement.",
        "The dashed Policy-to-KV-Index edge applies only when the selected policy is kv_aware."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Control plane",
      "items": [
        "Workers can be static (--worker-urls, --prefill, --decode) or discovered at runtime.",
        "Kubernetes service discovery watches pods and registers Regular / Prefill / Decode workers. vLLM ZMQ discovery (NCCL / MoRI-IO) registers HTTP and ZMQ addresses for PD.",
        "WorkerRegistry runs periodic health checks. Optional intra-node data-parallel expansion addresses workers as host:port@dp_rank."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Security and supporting features",
      "items": [
        "Bearer validation runs only when API_KEY_VALIDATION_URLS / --api-key-validation-urls is set; otherwise the HTTP API does not require a token. Successful tokens are cached in process.",
        "Workers have retries and circuit breakers. Prometheus metrics default to 0.0.0.0:29000. OpenTelemetry tracing is optional.",
        "Not drawn: optional WASM OnRequest middleware, Program scheduling, E+PD encoder orchestration, IGW RouterManager, and the OpenAI-backend single-base-URL mode."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
